From 73ce9d87dd5c345688ee5d21b84a07f556921f5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:29:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: leave native Dolby Vision when the flips of
 its frames do not come

A frame of native Dolby Vision output that the kernel refuses counts towards the return to the
ordinary output (DVBridgeFrameShown()). A frame whose commit is taken but whose flip never comes
was counted as shown: the commit returns all the same once the driver gives up waiting for the
flip, after 10 s with the kernel's helpers (amdgpu, i915: "flip_done timed out") and after 3 s
with nvidia-drm ("Flip event timeout"). Such an output shows nothing new while Kodi waits that
long for every frame: the GUI does not move, the sound goes on, and the player finds no free
picture buffer ("OutputPicture - timeout waiting for buffer"), the symptom that a user of another
Dolby Vision build reported on a Radeon 780M with the GUI at 4K 120 Hz.

CDVPresentStall tells it. Of the frames whose commit changes nothing but the picture (the
transport is on, and Kodi has asked for nothing else since the frame before), one that takes 2 s
or more stalled; two in a row, or one of 5 s or more (only the 10 s of the kernel's helpers take
that long), end native output for the video as a failure does (DisableNativeDVOutput(),
EndDVBridge()): the ordinary output takes over, whose own flips that do not come are dealt with
since kodi-9207. The first frame of a native output and the commits that carry a modeset do not
count, either way: setting the link up may take seconds.

A host test runs the policy at every rate of the transport, with frames in time and hiccups of
1.5 s that never end native output, nvidia-drm's 3 s and the helpers' 10 s, the thresholds, and
six mutations that make it fail.
